  "content": {
    "id": "p35-q29",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "29",
    "prompt": "Which term of the sequence $8,-4,2,\\ldots$ is $\\frac{1}{128}$?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "11th term.",
      "worked": "$a=8$, $r=-\\frac12$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a_n&=ar^{n-1}\\\\\\frac{1}{128}&=8\\left(-\\frac12\\right)^{n-1}\\\\\\frac{1}{1024}&=\\left(-\\frac12\\right)^{n-1}\\\\\\left(\\frac12\\right)^{10}&=\\left(-\\frac12\\right)^{n-1}\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor this to be true, $n-1$ must be even and\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac12\\right)^{n-1}&=\\left(\\frac12\\right)^{10}\\\\n-1&=10\\\\n&=11.\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{1}{128}$ is the 11th term.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 58
  },
